{
  "id": "COMPOUND:15061 - PROTEIN:5781",
  "verbalization": "Chaxamycin B appears to exert its biological effect through a series of molecular interactions involving the sialyltransferase CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase. This enzyme is a target of multiple compounds, including 2-Methylheptyl propanoate and (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan, which in turn targets A2780cisR. The consistent involvement of this sialyltransferase in the target pathways suggests a potential mechanism by which Chaxamycin B modulates the expression or activity of A2780cisR, likely through interference with sialylation processes. The evidence supports a role for Chaxamycin B in influencing the sialyltransferase pathway, which may have implications for cellular functions related to sialylation and its downstream effects on cell behavior. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of sialyltransferases in the biological response to Chaxamycin B, offering a plausible mechanism for its interaction with A2780cisR.",
